<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49022" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trīceps</span></b> ,
			cĭpĭtis, adj.
		tres-caput; cf. <i><span class="en">Cic. Or. 48, 159</span></i>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>having three
			heads</i>, <i>triple-headed</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cerberus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Tusc. 1, 5, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hecate (because she was also at the same time
					Luna and Diana),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 194</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>threefold</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">historia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 148</span></i>
			 Müll.</div>
